course: dictionary
lesson: 13243
title: Words about place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word geographical comes from geography, the study of the Earth: its places, land, seas, weather and people. When you meet geographical, ask yourself: is this about the Earth, or about where something is? «The class studied the geographical features of Wales, such as its mountains, rivers and coasts.» Features are the parts of the land you can see, so geographical features are the natural shapes and places on the land.
explain: «Our teacher showed us the geographical location of the school on a large map.» Location means where something is, so geographical location means exactly where a place sits on the Earth. Try the swap: "the place where the school is on a map" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Geographical is an adjective, so it describes a noun. You will see it in phrases like geographical area and geographical skills. «Ella used a compass to practise her geographical skills.» Skills like reading maps and using compasses are geographical because they help you understand the Earth.
fact: Geographical means to do with geography: the places, land, seas, climate and people of the Earth.
fact: Geographical features are natural parts of the land, such as mountains, rivers and coasts.
fact: Geographical location means where something is.
fact: A geographical area is a part of the Earth, such as a region, a valley or an island.
fact: Geographical skills include using maps and compasses.
exercise: «The class learned the geographical features of Scotland, such as its lochs and hills.» What does geographical mean here? | *To do with the land, seas and places of the Earth | To do with cooking food | To do with music and singing | To do with maths sums
exercise: «Ella used a compass to practise her geographical skills.» Which of these is a geographical skill? | Playing the piano | Baking bread | Painting a portrait | *Reading a map
exercise: Find the phrase that means a place on the Earth where something is. | geographical cake | *geographical location | geographical music | geographical game
test: «The team measured the geographical area of the new national park.» What is a geographical area? | A type of cloud | *A part of the Earth, such as a region or valley | A small room in a school | A kind of sports game
test: Which words describe the natural shapes of the land? | geographical songs | *geographical features | geographical lessons | geographical jokes
exam: «Our teacher showed us the geographical location of the school on a map.» What does geographical location mean? | The name of the teacher | How many pupils are in the class | *Where something is on the Earth | The time the school bell rings
